# Backend runtime environment.
#
# Copy to `backend/.env` (git-ignored) and fill in the values you need.
# spring-dotenv loads `backend/.env` into the Spring Environment on
# `./mvnw spring-boot:run`. In CI / containers, set these as real OS
# environment variables instead.
#
# Every key below is OPTIONAL except PINATA_JWT — `application.yml` has safe
# local defaults for the rest (and the repo-root `.env.example` documents the
# full catalogue, incl. the docker-compose Postgres settings).

# --- Pinata / IPFS (Audit Trail evidence) -----------------------------------
# READ-ONLY. A BACKEND-ONLY SECRET: never put it in the frontend, Vercel, or
# git. Blank => GET /api/audit/{id}/photos returns { "configured": false } and
# the Audit page shows a "not connected" note instead of an error.
PINATA_JWT=
# PINATA_NETWORK=public
# PINATA_GATEWAY_BASE_URL=https://gateway.pinata.cloud/ipfs/
# PINATA_EVIDENCE_LIMIT=2

# --- Overrides for application.yml defaults (only if the defaults don't fit) --
# MPLADS_DB_URL=jdbc:postgresql://localhost:5544/mpladsentinel
# MPLADS_DB_USERNAME=mpladsentinel
# MPLADS_DB_PASSWORD=change-me-locally
# MPLADS_AUTH_SEED_PASSWORD=Demo@12345
# MPLADS_CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173
# MPLADS_INGEST_RUN_ON_STARTUP=sample
